M.TOPICS["components"] = [[
# Components

A **Component** is a Frame with `reusable = true`. `Copy` of it makes an **Instance**, which draws the Component and follows every later change to it, with its own overrides on top. Use Components for anything that repeats: buttons, fields, toggles, cards, nav items, list rows, metrics.

## When and how to make one

- Make a Component as soon as a widget appears twice. Build it once, check it, then place Instances.
- Make one generic Component that Instances adapt (a label, an icon, a colour), not near-duplicates. Make states that change the structure (a button with and without an icon, a filled and an empty field) separate Components.
- Name variants with slashes: `Button/Primary`, `Button/Secondary`, `Field/Error`. The name says what it is, not what it looks like.
- For a component that changes when clicked (a switch, a checkbox, tabs, an accordion), make a variant set with `MakeVariants` and link its members: see "Interactive components" in `design_guide { topic = "prototyping" }`.
- Give the Component's inner nodes clear, unique names (`Label`, `Icon`), since Instances override them by name.
- Size Components by their content (`fit_content`) or to fill their parent, so Instances adapt to where they're placed. Fixed pixel widths are for things that really are fixed (an avatar, an icon button).
- Keep Components together on the Canvas, away from the Screens, and placed with `FindEmptySpace`.
- Build from Tokens, so a Theme change reaches every Instance.

```luau
SetTokens({
  primary = { type = "color", value = "#2563EB" },
  ["on-primary"] = { type = "color", value = "#FFFFFF" },
  surface = { type = "color", value = "#FFFFFF" },
  border = { type = "color", value = "#E4E4E7" },
  fg = { type = "color", value = "#18181B" },
  muted = { type = "color", value = "#71717A" },
  ["radius-pill"] = { type = "number", value = 999 },
  ["radius-md"] = { type = "number", value = 10 },
})
local label = { type = "text", name = "Label", fontSize = 14, fontWeight = 600 }
local continueLabel = table.clone(label); continueLabel.content = "Continue"; continueLabel.fill = "$on-primary"
G.primary = Insert({ type = "frame", name = "Button/Primary", reusable = true, x = 0, y = 0, layout = "horizontal", gap = 8,
  padding = { 10, 16 }, alignItems = "center", cornerRadius = "$radius-pill", fill = "$primary", children = {
    continueLabel,
    { type = "icon", name = "Icon", icon = "lucide:arrow-right", width = 16, height = 16, fill = "$on-primary" },
  } })
local spot = FindEmptySpace({ width = 120, height = 40, from = G.primary, padding = 24 })
local cancelLabel = table.clone(label); cancelLabel.content = "Cancel"; cancelLabel.fill = "$fg"
G.secondary = Insert({ type = "frame", name = "Button/Secondary", reusable = true, x = spot.x, y = spot.y, layout = "horizontal", gap = 8,
  padding = { 10, 16 }, alignItems = "center", cornerRadius = "$radius-pill", fill = "$surface",
  stroke = { fill = "$border", thickness = 1 }, children = { cancelLabel } })
TakeScreenshot({ G.primary, G.secondary })
```

## Placing and customising Instances

- Override the Instance's own properties directly in the Copy (`fill`, `width`, `x`).
- Override nodes inside it with `descendants`, keyed by the inner node's id in the Component, by its name when only one node has it, or by a slash path through a nested Instance (`buttonId/labelId`). A later `Update(instance, { descendants = … })` merges into the overrides it has (`null` drops one; `{ replace = true }` as the third argument replaces them all). Find an inner node of one Instance with `FindByName("Label", instance)`.
- A descendant given properties has them set; given a whole node with a `type`, it's replaced by that node.
- Hide an inner node with `enabled = false`. You can't Insert into, Move or Delete nodes inside an Instance.
- Set overrides as you Copy: the new Instance's ids aren't known until the call returns.
- Later, reach an inner node with `instanceId/nodeId` in `Get`, `Update` and `Replace`.

```luau
local spot = FindEmptySpace({ width = 400, height = 200 })
local screen = Insert({ type = "frame", name = "Dialog", x = spot.x, y = spot.y, width = 400,
  layout = "vertical", gap = 24, padding = 24, cornerRadius = 16, fill = "$surface", stroke = { fill = "$border", thickness = 1 } })
Insert(screen, { type = "text", name = "Question", content = "Archive this project?", fontSize = 18, fontWeight = 600, fill = "$fg", width = "fill_container" })
G.actions = Insert(screen, { type = "frame", name = "Actions", width = "fill_container", layout = "horizontal", gap = 12, justifyContent = "end" })
Copy(G.secondary, G.actions, {})
G.archive = Copy(G.primary, G.actions, { fill = "#DC2626", descendants = { Label = { content = "Archive" }, Icon = { enabled = false } } })
TakeScreenshot(screen)
```

```luau
local inner = Get(G.archive, { expandInstances = true, depth = 1 })
local lines = {}
for _, child in inner.children do
  table.insert(lines, `{child.id} {child.name} {if child.enabled == false then "hidden" else ""}`)
end
Print(lines)
local labelId = Get(G.primary).children[1].id
Update(`{G.archive}/{labelId}`, { content = "Archive project" })
```

## Nested Components

A Component can hold Instances of other Components. Reach through them with slash paths, both in `descendants` and in edits.

```luau
local buttonLabel = Get(G.primary).children[1].id
local spot = FindEmptySpace({ width = 280, height = 200, from = G.primary, direction = "bottom" })
G.card = Insert({ type = "frame", name = "Card/Plan", reusable = true, x = spot.x, y = spot.y,
  width = 280, layout = "vertical", gap = 12, padding = 24, cornerRadius = "$radius-md", fill = "$surface", stroke = { fill = "$border", thickness = 1 },
  children = {
    { type = "text", name = "Plan", content = "Starter", fontSize = 14, fontWeight = 600, fill = "$muted" },
    { type = "text", name = "Price", content = "$12", fontSize = 32, fontWeight = 600, fill = "$fg" },
  } })
G.cta = Copy(G.primary, G.card, { width = "fill_container", justifyContent = "center" })
local proSpot = FindEmptySpace({ width = 280, height = 200, from = G.card, padding = 40 })
local pro = Copy(G.card, nil, { x = proSpot.x, y = proSpot.y,
  descendants = { Plan = { content = "Pro" }, Price = { content = "$29" }, [`{G.cta}/{buttonLabel}`] = { content = "Go Pro" } } })
TakeScreenshot({ G.card, pro })
```

## Changing Components

- Change the Component, never each Instance, when the change should reach everywhere: every Instance follows, under its overrides.
- Read every Instance's overrides (`Get` on the Instance shows its `descendants`) before restructuring a Component: renaming or deleting an inner node orphans overrides that name it.
- To detach one Instance from its Component, Replace it with a plain Frame copied from what `Get(id, { expandInstances = true, depth = math.huge })` read.

```luau
Update(G.primary, { padding = { 12, 20 } })
TakeScreenshot({ G.primary, G.card })
```
]]

M.TOPICS["design-systems"] = [[
# Design systems

A design system here is a Design's Tokens and Themes plus a set of Components built only from them, laid out on the Canvas so a person (or another chat) can read it. Build it before the Screens that use it, or extract it from Screens that already exist.

## Order

1. Read what's there: `GetTokens()` and the Components on the Canvas. Existing Tokens are binding; extend them, and replace them (`{ replace = true }`) only when asked to.
2. Write the Tokens: colours with a light and dark value, then type, radius and spacing.
3. Build the core Components from the Tokens, one family per call, each checked with a screenshot.
4. Lay them out on the Canvas in labelled rows, so the system reads as a reference sheet.

## Tokens

Name Tokens by role, not by colour: `primary`, not `blue-600`. A useful set:

- Surfaces: `background`, `card`, `popover`.
- Text: `foreground`, `muted-foreground`.
- Lines: `border`, `input`, `ring` (focus).
- Actions: `primary`, `primary-foreground`, `secondary`, `secondary-foreground`, `destructive`, `destructive-foreground`.
- Status, each a background and a foreground: `success`, `warning`, `error`, `info`.
- Type: `font-primary` (headings, labels, navigation) and `font-secondary` (body, inputs); sizes as numbers if the scale matters.
- Radius: none for tables and dense data; medium for cards and dialogs; a pill for buttons, inputs and badges.
- Spacing: the scale's steps, when you'll use them as numbers (`["space-4"] = 16`).

Give a colour Token one value per Theme (`{ { value, theme = { mode = "light" } }, { value, theme = { mode = "dark" } } }`), after naming the axis with `SetThemes`; numbers and strings usually don't vary. The first value of each axis is what nodes show unless a node sets `theme`.

```luau
local function themed(light, dark)
  return { type = "color", value = { { value = light, theme = { mode = "light" } }, { value = dark, theme = { mode = "dark" } } } }
end
SetThemes("mode", { "light", "dark" })
SetTokens({
  background = themed("#FFFFFF", "#09090B"),
  card = themed("#FFFFFF", "#18181B"),
  foreground = themed("#09090B", "#FAFAFA"),
  ["muted-foreground"] = themed("#71717A", "#A1A1AA"),
  border = themed("#E4E4E7", "#27272A"),
  primary = themed("#18181B", "#FAFAFA"),
  ["primary-foreground"] = themed("#FAFAFA", "#18181B"),
  info = themed("#EFF6FF", "#172554"),
  ["info-foreground"] = themed("#1D4ED8", "#BFDBFE"),
  ["font-primary"] = { type = "string", value = "Geist" },
  ["font-secondary"] = { type = "string", value = "Geist" },
  ["radius-md"] = { type = "number", value = 8 },
  ["radius-pill"] = { type = "number", value = 999 },
})
Print(GetTokens().themes)
```

## The core set

Most product UI is built from: button variants (primary, secondary, outline, ghost, destructive), an input with its label and help text, a card, a sidebar with item states, tabs, a dropdown or list item, a table row and cell, pagination, an alert, and a dialog. Build what the product needs from this list, not all of it.

Recipes that hold up:

- **Card**: a header (title and one line of description), the content, then actions aligned right.
- **Sidebar**: a brand header, items grouped under small section labels with one item active, the user at the bottom.
- **Tabs**: a row of labels with the first active, marked by weight and a line or a filled pill.
- **Dropdown**: an optional search, items with a check on the chosen one, dividers between groups, small group titles.
- **Pagination**: previous and next, a few page numbers, an ellipsis for the gap.
- **Form**: short fields side by side (first and last name), then full-width fields.
- **Metric**: a muted label over a large value (about 32, semibold), then a small change indicator.
- **Alert**: an icon, a title and one sentence, in a status colour pair.

Where actions go: bottom right in cards, dialogs and forms; in toolbars, the primary on the left and the rest on the right; in a destructive dialog, Cancel then the destructive action, on the right.

```luau
G.alert = Insert({ type = "frame", name = "Alert/Info", reusable = true, x = 0, y = 0, width = 420, layout = "horizontal", gap = 12,
  padding = 16, cornerRadius = "$radius-md", fill = "$info", children = {
    { type = "icon", name = "Icon", icon = "lucide:info", width = 20, height = 20, fill = "$info-foreground" },
    { type = "frame", name = "Text", width = "fill_container", layout = "vertical", gap = 4, children = {
      { type = "text", name = "Title", content = "Heads up", fontFamily = "$font-primary", fontSize = 14, fontWeight = 600, fill = "$info-foreground", width = "fill_container" },
      { type = "text", name = "Body", content = "Your trial ends in three days.", fontFamily = "$font-secondary", fontSize = 14, lineHeight = 1.45, fill = "$info-foreground", width = "fill_container" },
    } },
  } })
local function item(name, icon, active)
  return { type = "frame", name = name, width = "fill_container", layout = "horizontal", gap = 10, padding = { 8, 12 },
    alignItems = "center", cornerRadius = "$radius-md", fill = if active then "$border" else "#00000000", children = {
      { type = "icon", name = "Icon", icon = icon, width = 16, height = 16, fill = if active then "$foreground" else "$muted-foreground" },
      { type = "text", name = "Label", content = name, fontSize = 14, fontWeight = if active then 600 else 400, fill = if active then "$foreground" else "$muted-foreground" },
    } }
end
local spot = FindEmptySpace({ width = 240, height = 200, from = G.alert, direction = "bottom", padding = 48 })
G.nav = Insert({ type = "frame", name = "Sidebar", x = spot.x, y = spot.y,
  width = 240, layout = "vertical", gap = 2, padding = 12, fill = "$card", stroke = { fill = "$border", thickness = 1 }, cornerRadius = "$radius-md",
  children = { item("Home", "lucide:house", true), item("Customers", "lucide:users", false), item("Settings", "lucide:settings", false) } })
TakeScreenshot({ G.alert, G.nav })
```

## Checking both Themes

Show the system in each Theme by copying a sheet with `theme` set, and screenshot both. Every text must keep its contrast in each.

```luau
local alertSpot = FindEmptySpace({ width = 420, height = 80, from = G.alert, padding = 48 })
local darkAlert = Copy(G.alert, nil, { x = alertSpot.x, y = alertSpot.y, theme = { mode = "dark" } })
local navSpot = FindEmptySpace({ width = 240, height = 200, from = G.nav, padding = 48 })
local darkNav = Copy(G.nav, nil, { x = navSpot.x, y = navSpot.y, theme = { mode = "dark" } })
TakeScreenshot({ darkAlert, darkNav })
```

## Rules

- Colours, type and radii in a Component come from Tokens. Small structural numbers (a 4 px gap between an icon and its label) can stay literal.
- One idea per card; tables of four to seven columns; reuse a Component before building a custom frame.
- When implementation follows, an HTML `Export` gives the Tokens as CSS custom properties at the top of its `<style>`, with each Theme under a data attribute (see the `code` topic guide).
]]

M.TOPICS["landing-pages"] = [[
# Landing pages

A landing page has one conversion goal (sign up, book a demo, download), and every section either moves the reader toward it or goes. Design at 1440 wide, as one Screen whose height grows with its sections (`height = "fit_content"`), built a section per call.

## Story

Write the copy before any visuals, in this arc:

1. **What it is**: the hero. One headline, one sentence of support, one call to action.
2. **Why it works**: three or four benefits, or how it works in steps.
3. **Proof**: numbers, logos (as wordmarks in type), quotes from real-sounding people with names and roles.
4. **The ask**: the call to action again, with any objection answered (price, trial, cancellation).

Headlines, strongest first: the change in the reader's life, a concrete result, a benefit, a feature. Lead with the strongest you can honestly claim, in eight words or fewer.

## Hero

- The headline is the largest thing on the page (56–88 on desktop), in the display face, tightened slightly (`letterSpacing` -1 to -2, `lineHeight` about 1.05).
- The call to action is the loudest element after it: the only filled accent button above the fold. A secondary action, if any, is a text link or outlined button.
- Say the offer, its value and the next step within the first screenful (about 800 px).
- You can't generate images. Use the person's images (by their http(s) URLs), or build the hero from type and colour: a bold colour block, an oversized number, a product mock made of Frames. Where an image belongs and none is given, reserve the area with a quiet fill and a small label saying what goes there.
- Text over an image always gets contrast help: a dark scrim, a gradient from the side the text is on, or a solid band. Images keep their proportions (`mode = "cover"`).

```luau
SetTokens({
  bg = { type = "color", value = "#F7F5F0" },
  ink = { type = "color", value = "#1A1814" },
  ["ink-muted"] = { type = "color", value = "#5F5A50" },
  accent = { type = "color", value = "#C2410C" },
  ["on-accent"] = { type = "color", value = "#FFFFFF" },
  band = { type = "color", value = "#1A1814" },
  ["font-display"] = { type = "string", value = "Instrument Serif" },
  ["font-text"] = { type = "string", value = "Geist" },
})
```

The photo here is one the person supplied, by its URL.

```luau
G.page = Insert({ type = "frame", name = "Landing", x = 0, y = 0, width = 1440, height = "fit_content", layout = "vertical", fill = "$bg", clip = true, inProgress = true })
G.hero = Insert(G.page, { type = "frame", name = "Hero", width = "fill_container", layout = "horizontal", gap = 64, padding = { 96, 120 }, alignItems = "center", children = {
  { type = "frame", name = "Copy", width = "fill_container", layout = "vertical", gap = 24, children = {
    { type = "text", name = "Headline", content = "Cook dinner in twenty minutes, every night", fontFamily = "$font-display", fontSize = 76, lineHeight = 1.02, letterSpacing = -1.5, fill = "$ink", width = "fill_container" },
    { type = "text", name = "Support", content = "Recipes planned around what is already in your kitchen, with one shopping list for the week.", fontFamily = "$font-text", fontSize = 19, lineHeight = 1.5, fill = "$ink-muted", width = "fill_container" },
    { type = "frame", name = "Actions", layout = "horizontal", gap = 20, alignItems = "center", children = {
      { type = "frame", name = "CTA", layout = "horizontal", gap = 8, padding = { 14, 24 }, cornerRadius = 999, fill = "$accent", alignItems = "center", children = {
        { type = "text", name = "CTA label", content = "Plan my week", fontFamily = "$font-text", fontSize = 16, fontWeight = 600, fill = "$on-accent" },
        { type = "icon", name = "CTA arrow", icon = "lucide:arrow-right", width = 18, height = 18, fill = "$on-accent" },
      } },
      { type = "text", name = "Reassurance", content = "Free for 14 days", fontFamily = "$font-text", fontSize = 15, fill = "$ink-muted" },
    } },
  } },
  { type = "frame", name = "Photo", width = 520, height = 600, cornerRadius = 24, clip = true, layout = "vertical", justifyContent = "end", padding = 24,
    fill = { { type = "image", url = "https://example.com/photos/miso-salmon.jpg", mode = "cover" }, { type = "gradient", rotation = 0, colors = { { color = "#000000AA", position = 0 }, { color = "#00000000", position = 0.5 } } } },
    children = { { type = "text", name = "Caption", content = "Tuesday: miso salmon, 18 minutes", fontFamily = "$font-text", fontSize = 15, fontWeight = 500, fill = "#FFFFFF" } } },
} })
TakeScreenshot(G.hero)
```

## Sections

- Each section chooses one alignment, left or centred, and keeps it.
- Alternate text-led and visual sections, and vary their structure: a three-column benefit row, then a wide split, then a dark band. A page of identical card grids reads as a template.
- Dark bands lend weight (proof, the final ask); light ones explain.
- Keep a consistent section rhythm: the same vertical padding (96–128) and the same content width.
- Benefits are short: a bold phrase and one sentence each, with an icon only if it carries meaning.

```luau
local function stat(value, label)
  return { type = "frame", name = label, width = "fill_container", layout = "vertical", gap = 8, children = {
